ligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x -6 & =12 -x \\\\ (2)x & =18 \\\\ x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=9$ into either of the two equations gives $y=3.$ So, our solution is $x=9$ and $y=3.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(9,3).$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(-3,15)$ and $(9,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2} \\\\ & =\\sqrt{(9-(-3))^2+(3-(15))^2} \\\\ & =\\sqrt{144+144} \\\\ & =12 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(-3,15)$ and the line $y=x -6$ is $12 \\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484370 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484371 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484377 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484382 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484384 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1077 "selection" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1078 #edb/ref 17592186484384 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484380 1079 #uuid "a3d1ccc5-b072-55cb-987e-f64512327d14" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484372 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484373 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484374 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484386 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484387 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484381 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [1759218648438