r and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3 x}{2} -21 & =\\frac{2 x}{3} -\\frac{35}{6} \\\\ (-\\frac{13}{6})x & =\\frac{91}{6} \\\\ x & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-7$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-\\frac{21}{2}.$ So, our solution is $x=-7$ and $y=-\\frac{21}{2}.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(-7,-\\frac{21}{2}).$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(14,\\frac{7}{2})$ and $(-7,-\\frac{21}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2} \\\\ & =\\sqrt{(-7-(14))^2+(-\\frac{21}{2}-(\\frac{7}{2}))^2} \\\\ & =\\sqrt{441+196} \\\\ & =7 \\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(14,\\frac{7}{2})$ and the line $3 x + 2 y=-42$ is $7 \\sqrt{13}.$" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484384 1080 "3 \\sqrt{29}" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484384 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484384 1083 #uuid "cb5cffb6-f40b-53a8-ba11-c1f8f059b0ac" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484385 1080 "24 \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484385 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484385 1083 #uuid "d014d8ac-e7ad-5b0e-8559-0c2bd1320040" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484386 1080 "14" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484386 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484386 1083 #uuid "d0a88fdc-c029-5c95-a46c-5983a3cf3b95" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484387 1080 "21" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484387 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484387 1083 #uuid "dfec296f-fcca-599e-821f-c9e9985dc17e" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484388 1080 "6" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484388 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [175921864843