aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=15 -\\frac{5 x}{2} \\\\ y=\\frac{2 x}{5} + 15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 -\\frac{5 x}{2} & =\\frac{2 x}{5} + 15 \\\\ (-\\frac{29}{10})x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$ into either of the two equations gives $y=15.$ So, our solution is $x=0$ and $y=15.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(0,15).$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(-15,9)$ and $(0,15):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2} \\\\ & =\\sqrt{(0-(-15))^2+(15-(9))^2} \\\\ & =\\sqrt{225+36} \\\\ & =3 \\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(-15,9)$ and the line $5 x + 2 y=30$ is $3 \\sqrt{29}.$" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484391 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186073811.py" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true] [17592186484391 1169 #uuid "3c694cc5-eb03-50d9-a8cb-abb3d249d370" 13194139535236 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"0a40b10b-7f8f-567c-b059-d1778d42ed93" 17592186484370 "1436d41a-008b-5d24-943f-6c6ada0e47b6" 17592186484371 "166e3f8c-f04b-5da1-9412-38ad97850cf3" 17592186484372 "25df8fdd-3126-5e6d-8151-85d7400b86ed" 17592186484373 "4922448d-3df4-5380-9f15-02e91d6305ff" 17592186484374 "6cae1362-ea07-5824-927c-25a4a487e098" 17592186484375 "7753ff6b-adb7-52b1-9810-10a100856790" 17592186484376 "7a63166c-3fbf-5cf1-ad6c-ccc4fd6560b8" 17592186484377 "7b72658c-4203-56e3-b013-04b826bee95e" 17592186484378 "99d5220d-0d33-5926-9ea0-c7324f7866f5" 17592186484379 "a3d1ccc5-b072-55cb-987e-f64512327d14" 17592186484380 "ad3073cb-e9f3-5964-919f-4f70383397a0" 17592186484381 "bf167359-bd5b-561f-83d8-a12dda3667ee" 17592186484382 "c182161a-7f52-5240-b03d-e600d3d24498" 17592186484383 "cb5cffb6-f40b-53a